[TEXT] **Found it.** The smoking gun is on **mswitch1**:

```
eth0.10@eth0: <BROADCAST,MULTICAST> mtu 1500 master br_vlan10 state DOWN
```

`mswitch1.eth0.10` is **DOWN** (bridge state: `disabled`), while the VLAN-20 counterpart `eth0.20@eth0` is **UP**. This is the exact interface in the VLAN-10 forwarding path between switch1 and router0. All other `br_vlan10` members on mswitch1 (`eth2.10`, `eth4.10`) are forwarding normally — the fault is isolated to this one sub-interface.

The team was looking on the wrong device (router0 instead of mswitch1), and at the correct VLAN (10) but the wrong hop.

